{"authored" [{"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,i+(2-t)\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i-\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4t}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+4t}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4t}}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}i-\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(3i+2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(i-\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\sqrt{t}\\,i-2t\\,j)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-\\,j)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩$ at the point $P(1,1,4)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,1,4)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩ \\\\ ⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4}=1 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ 4t=4.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, we get $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(1,1,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3},\\,2(1),\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(1,1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $t=\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\pi )^{2}+(0)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}\\pi )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi ) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\pi )}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b7