e/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(2,1,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,1,1)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k \\\\ 2t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k & =2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ t=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2,1,1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2t\\,j+\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =2\\,i+2(1)\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\,j+\\frac{1}{3}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,j+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33584" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={e}^{-t}p(t)$ at the point where $t=0$, if $p(0)=\\,i+\\,j+k$ and ${p}^{′}(0)=\\,i-\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})p(t)+{e}^{-t}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}p(t)+{e}^{-t}{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{0}p(0)+{e}^{0}{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-(\\,i+\\,j+k)+(\\,i-\\,j) \\\\  & =-2j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}(-2j-k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is $T(0)=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "99c2b742170bdfe85e4821385cdb906e0c6526ef8df09e7b1c8d64ea217c289a" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b540fddcfd6785c097a10ba16e3ca8c0ccf88ad0f4e7e13d69141d678f8d7b4" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle \\sin^3{t}, \\:\\cos^3{t} \\right\\rangle$ at an arbitrary point where $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/example-3055.json" "file_sha256" "3561411f6f0388be3be00ef7cde3f26299aa392c64661f5e493e98c9da61af02" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $\\mathbf r(t)= x(t) \\,\\mathbf i + y(t) \\,\\mathbf j,$ the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(t)=\\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\right\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{3}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({cos}^{3}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{cos}^{2}⁡t(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf r'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\ \\text{ } & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the last step, we were able to remove the absolute value bars because $\\sin{t}>0$ and $\\cos{t}>0$ for $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we normalize $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/questio