-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/ff0324d951fb404b12736c08195532ce8d2fe57cae5baf845673b3626b871eb6.png) \n\nFirst, we find the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/7a5dc70352bd991ad75358cc62cef8d67afbb5cb00da1578f008a0b392d2385d.png) that corresponds to the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/83fbafba1d5d5be0d132254724f1cadcd31c51dc923c63113d0f393bf6bf94bc.png) on the given curve. We know that\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/aebba9c47fe0ea053b4fc1924e7f3a97ee17dc60fc074091ba0f6c303301cfda.png)\nIn the above equation, the first component in each of the two vectors is equal to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/549c2a20cf7ec79cb4b26e39d950105c670a74452b2d7d024d3d5e64d553ecbe.png) Equating the other two components gives the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/187d4f3cd4d27fdac888ccf0d88c58f0cfb073913999f5767584476d9d2d4e10.png)\nFrom the first equation, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/02ad803439ddfa163c4788fb00ff86c65d3e0dc0711af87290695a8f06471e81.png) This value satisfies the second equation too. Therefore, the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/3d4f13f8fb24239874d83180ba75954be6d86ec8bb6e339bea3a0c1c9a4edae4.png) is at the tip of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/7479ebb2b1c8ed8146f6833341d2e732dcd91f86781823d36906dd19cadca82c.png) \n\nNow, we calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/2a03e92cf496f1508de5344917e1f5fe5574f9801a0ef229649288a29c15044b.png) and evaluate it at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/06f646a39990b7ed47b7ab431b54ea320a05650e5e4f6df6f51812460536154b.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/9432511f61bf63030d95771cdc107682a61444fe925dab681ab8388b4a48524e.png) \n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/3b10ec5094240cfd7f221bc22e19a29d74b4a69d2788887265041cc7db5291ca.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/ff9d6534ce414a2151a6dbbe2d407328ed6514447608f8601dfed6a1de27471c.png)\n\nFinally, we normalize ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/e9ece600ee31f7dc6e24c0639da455b0bba4fc3a7765986b08473109a93f0883.png) and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/5deae1091d1cd3c2502da1214919e0520c8cbe620d0ae3c2f1f926caf52f3cc0.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/f110fc18608eb66b7f1927adb60049b76390669485638da4cddd592e23738998.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/example-3054.json" "file_sha256" "68229a275409fac4a8c441245885181942605d93d5ef27b8ba79c4762449d1ed" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=e^{2t}\\mathbf p(t)$ at the point where $t=0,$ if $\\mathbf p(0)=\\mathbf i-\\,\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k$ and $\\mathbf p'(0)=\\mathbf i - \\mathbf j+ 2\\mathbf k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/example-3056.json" "file_sha256" "f2fd39dbf95ccc4f10eb196d3e9baf5da6cae1bdd9763089b70ba9437a682e1a" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-3056" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $\\mathbf r(t)=x(t)\\mathbf i+y(t)\\mathbf j+z(t)\\mathbf k,$ the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(t)=\\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\right\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})p(t)+{e}^{2t}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}p(t)+{e}^{2t}{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =2{e}^{2(0)}p(0)+{e}^{2(0)}{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =2(i-\\,j-k)+1(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =3\\,i-3\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf r'(0)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot {3}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $\\mathbf r'(0)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}(3\\,i-3\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i-j) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is $\\mathbf T(0) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\mathbf i -  \\mathbf j).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/example-3056.json" "file_sha256" "f2fd39dbf95ccc4f10eb196d3e9baf5da6cae1bdd9763089b70ba9437a682e1a" "basis" 1754 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=({t}^{2}+2)p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=-1$, given that  $p(-1)=i+2\\,j-k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(-1)=i+\\,j-\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=-1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(({t}^{2}+2)p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2)\\cdot p(t)+({t}^{2}+2)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =2t\\,p(t)+({t}^{2}+2)\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(-1) & =2(-1)\\,p(-1)+((-1)^{2}+2)\\,{p}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =-2\\,p(-1)+3\\,{p}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =-2(i+2\\,j-k)+3(i+\\,j-\\,k) \\\\  & =-2i-4\\,j+2k+3i+3j-3\\,k \\\\  & =i-j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(-1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(-1)}{‖{r}^{′}(-1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot (i-j-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(i-j-k)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=-1$ is  $T(-1)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(i-j-k).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fcece3a3d2624c5c2cc21a908b0507a8a567e3989bda04ada700b8f5ef127a8e" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}(i-j-k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(-2i+3j-2k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(i-j-k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}(-2i+j+k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-75148" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}(i+2j-k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, given that  $p(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{3}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\cdot p(t)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t\\,p(t)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})p(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}){p}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2(i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k)+(1)(\\sqrt{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =(2\\,i-3\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\,k)+\\sqrt{3}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-3\\,j+2\\sqrt{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖ & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9+12} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (2\\,i-3\\,j+2\\sqrt{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n $T(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fcece3a3d2624c5c2cc21a908b0507a8a567e3989bda04ada700b8f5ef127a8e" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c3