answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{1}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2}{5}\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/state.json" "file_sha256" "866e0d1304c6387c300668b16893c09035c3bb49ff88dfe6afa10d5f3a7d967c" "basis" 2052 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063094/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-127217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the unit tangent vector to the curve\n $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t),\\,z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+{(-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64{cos}^{2}⁡2t+64{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+16({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+16} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{17}}⟨2,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨1,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-127217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{17}⟨1,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨1,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨{t}^{2},\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{17}⟨t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨1,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}(\\,i+2t\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-33075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}}(\\,i+t\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}(\\,i+2t\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}(\\,i-2t\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}(t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}(\\,i+t\\,j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}(\\,i+2t\\,j)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-74894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-74894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-74894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-74894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-74894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2+{t}^{2}}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-74894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,i+(2-t)\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i-\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4t}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1+4t}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{1+4t}}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}i-\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(3i+2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{1+4t}(i-\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(\\sqrt{t}\\,i-2t\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-\\,j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4t}}(i-2\\sqrt{t}\\,j)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+5t\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+5\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}}(2t\\,i+5\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-127211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4{t}^{2}+25}(t\\,i+2\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4{t}^{2}+25}(t\\,i+5\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}}(2t\\,i+5\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}}(t\\,i+5{t}^{2}\\,j)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+5}}(2t\\,i+5\\,j)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}}(2t\\,i+5\\,j)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $t=\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{3}t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\pi )^{2}+(0)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}\\pi )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi ) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\pi )}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\pi }⟨-\\pi ,\\,0,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{7}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{7}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{12}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{12}},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{12}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33136" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\,0,\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩$ at the point $P(1,1,4)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(1,1,4)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩ \\\\ ⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4}=1 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ 4t=4.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equality, we get $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(1,1,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2t,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3},\\,2(1),\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(1,1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨4,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33655" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ at the point $P(2\\pi ,1,0)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2\\pi ,1,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\pi \\,i+\\,j+0\\,k \\\\ t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k & =2\\pi \\,i+\\,j+0\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}t=2\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t=1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=2\\pi .$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2\\pi ,1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(2\\pi ).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=2\\pi :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(2\\pi ) & =\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =i+0\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =i+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(2\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(2\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+0+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(2\\pi )$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2\\pi ,1,0):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2\\pi ) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(2\\pi )}{‖{r}^{′}(2\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot (i+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-33063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k"]] "ca