t)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡t\\,p(t)+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})p(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}){p}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2(i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k)+(1)(\\sqrt{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =(2\\,i-3\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\,k)+\\sqrt{3}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-3\\,j+2\\sqrt{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖ & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9+12} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (2\\,i-3\\,j+2\\sqrt{3}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n $T(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2}{3}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,i-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{21}}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{1}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2}{5}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-127274" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={e}^{-t}p(t)$ at the point where $t=0$, if $p(0)=\\,i+\\,j+k$ and ${p}^{′}(0)=\\,i-\\,j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})p(t)+{e}^{-t}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =-{e}^{-t}p(t)+{e}^{-t}{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =-{e}^{0}p(0)+{e}^{0}{p}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =-(\\,i+\\,j+k)+(\\,i-\\,j) \\\\  & =-2j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(0)}{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}(-2j-k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=0$ is $T(0)=-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b896077b3f61a65625294d246f92b173da2405f8e0fe554beffd6b1050162333"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}i-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}i-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "q-33096" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}j-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/state.json" "file_sha256" "a99ed71a27136f5ef5e49f4dbd51c5bf2873e2fa91388ce32dda9ee4be53f53a"} {"question" "e-3055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle \\sin^3{t}, \\:\\cos^3{t} \\right\\rangle$ at an arbitrary point where $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/example-3055.json" "file_sha256" "3561411f6f0388be3be00ef7cde3f26299aa392c64661f5e493e98c9da61af02"} {"question" "e-3055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve $\\mathbf r(t)= x(t) \\,\\mathbf i + y(t) \\,\\mathbf j,$ the unit tangent vector $\\mathbf T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(t)=\\dfrac{\\mathbf r'(t)}{\\left\\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\right\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{3}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({cos}^{3}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{cos}^{2}⁡t(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf r'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\ \\text{ } & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =|3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|\\sqrt{1} \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the last step, we were able to remove the absolute value bars because $\\sin{t}>0$ and $\\cos{t}>0$ for $0 < t < \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we normalize $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩}{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/example-3055.json" "file_sha256" "3561411f6f0388be3be00ef7cde3f26299aa392c64661f5e493e98c9da61af02"} {"question" "e-3054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/assets/1a5a0925f4e15e00c9eff4bb4f39ce9c6eda232881bbddb07184ac54bbc269a8.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/assets/1e24125540d8b43cf8d314684fef6fb5be15c62d6988f9aac984f9812e6a74fd.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/example-3054.json" "file_sha256" "4b5ad9a958d27f14dfa03781483bd3e942e20df39d50c4636d2a55a24b404b8f"} {"question" "e-3054" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/assets/19e0e7fd4e5fd8c87c47e91b925dbad3eb9f4d5be314a38fec833931bd4ef4af.png) the unit tangent vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/assets/87516be3064aee2f19b0c6f7a771edef5c421